  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is currently addressing allegations of illegal wiretapping targeting President Prabowo Subianto. These claims have prompted significant legislative interest, with members of the House of Representatives advocating for a thorough and transparent police investigation to safeguard national cybersecurity and privacy. In response, the National Police have initiated formal ethics proceedings against involved parties, including civil servants and a police inspector general. Furthermore, the National Police Chief recently announced the rotation of two high-ranking police commissioners while the investigation proceeds. External observers, including the Indonesia Police Watch, have publicly urged authorities to handle the inquiry with accountability. Meanwhile, the Witness and Victim Protection Agency is evaluating reports of threats directed toward six individuals who are reportedly acting as witnesses in the ongoing criminal probe. The matter has also been formally addressed during parliamentary plenary sessions.",
